# Brand tokens

Phase 1 of every Figma build. Do not restyle buttons or compose pages until `src/brand.ts` matches the file.

`src/brand.ts` is the only look file. `CustomStyles.astro` injects `brandStylesheet()`. `astro.config.ts` reads `brandFontConfig()` for Google Fonts.

## From Figma

- If the file has Variables or a Design System frame: copy color, type, and radius into `brand`.
- If it does not: walk a few representative frames, collect the most-used fills, text styles (family, weight, size), and corner radius. Map those into `brand.colors`, `brand.fonts`, `brand.radius`. Do not create a token per one-off swatch.

## Type

Map Figma styles into `brand.type` roles, then only use `Heading` / `Text` (or `text-h1`–`text-h4`). Never hardcode `text-[52px]` in widgets.

| Role | Use |
|---|---|
| `h1` | Hero / display |
| `h2` | Section heading |
| `h3` | Pullquote / numbered title |
| `h4` | Card / subsection title |
| `body-lg` | Lede, hero subtitle |
| `body` | Paragraph |
| `eyebrow` | All-caps label |
| `small` | Card body, footnotes |
| `caption` | Metadata |

**Prefer Figma.** Most files ship a design system for **desktop and mobile**. Copy both:

- `size` ← desktop (usually 1440)
- `mobile` ← phone / mobile type styles

Do **not** invent mobile sizes when Figma already has them.

**Fallback only** if there is no mobile type (no mobile Variables, no mobile Design System, no mobile text styles):

- `h1.mobile` ≈ 50% of desktop `h1`
- `h2.mobile` ≈ 60% of desktop `h2`
- `h3.mobile` ≈ 65% of desktop `h3`
- `h4.mobile` ≈ 80% of desktop `h4`
- `body`, `bodyLg`, `button`, `eyebrow`, `small`, `caption` — same as desktop

This file used that fallback (100/52/36/28 → 48/32/24/22) because the Figma file had desktop type only.

## In code

- Components and pages use Tailwind tokens / CSS variables (`text-heading`, `text-muted`, `bg-card-dark`, `bg-section-grey`, `bg-cta`, `text-accent`).
- Never hardcode hex (`#222`, `#FAFAFA`, gold, navy) in widgets or pages.
- Changing a site's look = edit `src/brand.ts` (plus logo/favicons). Do not add a visual-system rule file per client.
- Name, URL, GTM, and Search Console live in `src/config/site.ts`. Phone and address live in `src/config/contact.ts`.
